    "congressionalg7391unit:207:par_000207_000040": {
      "text": "Sec. 3. And be it further enacted, That in further enforcement of the provision of the Constitution pro- hibiting slavery, and in order to remove all relics of this wrong from the States where this constitutional prohibition takes effect, it is hereby declared that all laws or customs in such States establishing any oli- garchical privileges and any distinction of rights on account of color or race are hereby annulled, and all persons in such States are recognized as equal be- fore the law; and the penalties provided in the last section are hereby made applicable to any violation of this provision, which is made in pursuance of the Constitution of the United States.",
